**who —** The Sleeper — the young man frozen before the End Day who wakes a century later with no memory — the player's hero, unnamed in canon (the NES default save-name is 'SNK'; the GBC remake names him Simea), who gathers the four swords and climbs the Tower

**what —** the young man frozen before the End Day who wakes a century later with no memory — the player's hero, unnamed in canon (the NES default save-name is 'SNK'; the GBC remake names him Simea), who gathers the four swords and climbs the Tower

**where —** XTL · Crystalis — SNK, NES 1990 (the US release of God Slayer, 1990)  Framework inputs: Crystalis; the four swords; the Tower; DYNA; the four sages; Mesia  Conductor / external anchor: ROOT0 (catalogued into UD0)

**why —** He is the world's blank witness: a man from the age of machines, woken into the age of magic that replaced them, carrying the forgotten past in a head wiped clean.

**how —** Crystallized from Crystalis (NES 1990) / God Slayer: Haruka Tenku no Sonata (1990).

**◌ the mythos —** He is the world's blank witness: a man from the age of machines, woken into the age of magic that replaced them, carrying the forgotten past in a head wiped clean. a being of the reborn world, the four swords, and the climb to DYNA

